# The repository is LF everywhere, in the working tree as well as in the
# object store.
#
# Two CI gates compare committed bytes against generated bytes:
# api/openapi.yaml and internal/api/client are what cmd/wtgen writes, and
# the artefact tests compare a rendered file against the copy committed in
# testdata/fixtures/plain-app. Every generator here writes \n. With a
# CRLF checkout — which is what `core.autocrlf=true`, the Git for Windows
# default, produces — each of those comparisons reports drift that does
# not exist, and `gofmt -l` lists every .go file in the tree.
#
# eol=lf is what makes a Windows checkout byte-identical to a Linux one.
* text=auto eol=lf
